<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav copper output up at 10,629 tonnes in Dec.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav copper output up at 10,629 tonnes in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following metla production details.</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION  DEC 96     NOV 96     DEC 95</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes) 10,629	8,759	5,959</p>
<p> refined lead			  930	1,925	  595</p>
<p> zinc				  2,516	3,435	1,428</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		  4,208	3,383	2,085</p>
<p> refined silver (kilos)	  4,996	4,877	5,226</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES    DEC 96     NOV 96     DEC 95</p>
<p> copper (thousand tonnes)	1,436	1,654	1,727</p>
<p> lead-zinc				65	   60	   62</p>
<p> bauxite				  35	   60	   --</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
